0|0@NoStupidQuestions^1440597582#cug8s72:BuddhaRocks$:"Proximity" or "hand-held" tasers only affect the person they are held against and must be close to work. "Firing" tasers work by wire at a distance. They use projected electrodes that transmit the electric shock through the clothing and into the muscles of the target. It is possible to receive a slight second-hand shock if you touch the person being tased. That shock will not have much effect unless the person's clothing is wet.
